“No strings on me.” — Ultron.

The distinction is between freedom from control and freedom from consequences.

You can reject a social contract, challenge its legitimacy, and work to change it. But autonomy isn’t the same as having power over everyone else’s choices.

And there’s a more interesting form of freedom: not merely breaking the strings, but becoming capable enough that nobody needs to pull them.

Self-mastery over obedience. Creation over destruction. Agency without domination.